1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:02,540
Is there a new dwarf
planet past Pluto?

2
00:00:03,360 --> 00:00:04,160
Maybe.

3
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:07,400
Chile's new Rubin
Observatory spotted an object

4
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:10,140
forty-six times farther
from the Sun than Earth.

5
00:00:11,240 --> 00:00:13,980
It might be up to fifteen
hundred kilometres wide.

6
00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:16,340
Why did nobody see it before?

7
00:00:16,780 --> 00:00:19,360
It sits in the southern
sky, in front of the crowded

8
00:00:19,360 --> 00:00:22,700
Milky Way, where one
slow dot gets lost.

9
00:00:23,880 --> 00:00:26,100
To be a dwarf planet,
it must be round.

10
00:00:26,720 --> 00:00:27,760
That still needs checking.
